From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kennytech73 <contact@bookworm-mon0.org>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: cdns3: guard against an unset host_dev or hcd in cdns_host_resume()

cdns_host_resume() reads the drvdata of cdns->host_dev unconditionally.
A runtime resume can run during probe, before the host role is started and
before xhci-plat has set its drvdata, so cdns->host_dev or the hcd can
still be NULL at that point. There is nothing to update yet in that case:
return early instead of dereferencing it.

Tested on an Orange Pi 6 Plus (CIX CD8180) with 6.18.14 and the Sky1
series.

Signed-off-by: kennytech73 <contact@bookworm-mon0.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/usb/cdns3/host.c | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/cdns3/host.c b/drivers/usb/cdns3/host.c
--- a/drivers/usb/cdns3/host.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/cdns3/host.c
@@ -140,9 +140,21 @@
 
 static int cdns_host_resume(struct cdns *cdns, bool power_lost)
 {
-	struct usb_hcd *hcd = platform_get_drvdata(cdns->host_dev);
-	struct xhci_plat_priv *priv = hcd_to_xhci_priv(hcd);
+	struct usb_hcd *hcd;
+	struct xhci_plat_priv *priv;
 
+	/*
+	 * Runtime resume can run during probe, before the host role is started
+	 * and xhci-plat has set its drvdata: nothing to update yet.
+	 */
+	if (!cdns->host_dev)
+		return 0;
+
+	hcd = platform_get_drvdata(cdns->host_dev);
+	if (!hcd)
+		return 0;
+
+	priv = hcd_to_xhci_priv(hcd);
 	priv->power_lost = power_lost;
 
 	return 0;
-- 
